# netsurf: position: fixed is sized and placed against the viewport; single-line flex containers sized by top/bottom centre their items
#
# - A fixed box's containing block is the viewport, not the nearest
#   positioned ancestor: YouTube fixes <body> while its consent dialog is
#   up, and the dialog sized itself to the 891 px body. layout_position_
#   absolute gives fixed boxes a viewport box at the document origin (redraw
#   and hit testing add the scroll, patch 112) and places them from their
#   parent's absolute position.
# - Only the OUTERMOST fixed box takes the scroll offset (a fixed box inside
#   a fixed <body> moved twice as far).
# - layout_flex re-read the container's CSS height (auto) and lost the
#   definite height layout_absolute set from top + bottom
#   (VB_DEFINITE_HEIGHT), so a full-screen "align-items: center" overlay left
